\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\n- ${C}_{1}:=…$\n- ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}$\n- ${C}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{43}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}: &={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-7{C}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48b1c21b-17a8-5932-8da9-5e616c8cd523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-4{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400494} {:answer/id #uuid "466954de-a984-57a2-be5a-cd8d17a4da88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-4{C}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400495} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7