x} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -8 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & -8 \\\\ -1 & 10 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}: &={C}_{4}+4{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 10 & 3 & 15\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f950a42d-a540-5921-9a3d-d668bd318fcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402830} {:answer/id #uuid "01d7bfc6-a04a-533c-8665-b132159f8eb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-3{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+4{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402831} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6ab905-f6c2-51df-be91-308b16286694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-2{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402832} {:answer/id #uuid "fc1548a5-d455-56f1-be69-1c079b40aef3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402833} {:answer/id #uuid "5a20cf7f-f569-51b2-9f0c-7247587435dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402830} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2400bde-d5f2-5b5e-81f0-94f5fae33cb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402829}] :question/id #uuid "abd07e98-c7c9-5953-be97-025190235f0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42562" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -5 & -3 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\nI. ${C}_{2}:=…$\nII. ${C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-5{C}_{1}$\nIII. ${C}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{1},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 8 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -5 & -3 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}: &={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -3 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}-5{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 7 & 8 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}: &={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{2}:={C}_{2}-4{C}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{1}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404537 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d5e36b83-15a1-5e52-9e6e-214c301a2528" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404539} {:answer/id #uuid "dd76300c-564c-55b8-901b-9e2bd1390ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-3{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404540} {:answer/id #uuid "49b5e613-99b1-573d-91c5-9e3ef4f411b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404541} {:answer/id #uuid "0aca2d4a-7507-5511-8293-17a03410d0d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404542} {:answer/id #uuid "eeae7dbd-76b9-5ceb-9da7-1df8844c0123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404541} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e62e048-fd08-5b04-8d22-e746ab71041b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404538}] :question/id #uuid "b9ef8afb-c422-57bc-a155-4bf0fc567ca9" :question/math-academy-id "q-91212" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & -24 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary column operations \n\nI. ${C}_{1}:=…$\nII. ${C}_{3}:=…$\nIII. ${C}_{4}:={C}_{4}-3{C}_{2}$\n\neach of the form ${C}_{i}:={C}_{i}+k{C}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary column operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{12}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary column operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}: &={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{3}: &={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & 4 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{4}: &={C}_{4}-3{C}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -16 & 8 & -16 & -20 \\\\ -12 & 9 & -17 & -24 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding elementary column operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${C}_{1}:={C}_{1}-2{C}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{C}_{3}:={C}_{3}-2{C}_{2}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Column Operations to Create a Row of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161967 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161759 :question/id #uuid "399b7598-c793-5032-9f33-ac02c7b85fe1" :question/math-academy-id "e-8050" :question/problem "\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{{\\color{blue}1}} & {\\color{blue}4} & {\\color{blue}-7} \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{{\\color{blue}1}} & {\\color{blue}4} & {\\color{blue}-7} \\\\ {\\color{red}0} & -6 & 6 \\\\ {\\color{red}0} & 10 & -20\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_i:=R_i+kR_1,$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below $a_{11}={\\color{blue}\\bbox[lightgray,2pt]{1}}$ equal to ${\\color{red}0}.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}: &={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 10 & -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\qquad$ $R_2:=R_2-2R_1\\quad$ and $\\quad R_3:=R_3+3R_1.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526485 :question-generator/id #uuid "6c1ecffd-0dfd-5a5a-bbd9-10ec41b53897" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186161967.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162553 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad6a43ec-d06a-5805-903a-7b82af563185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160611} {:answer/id #uuid "ee487a48-c57f-5440-953d-2e1a0b29979d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160612} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8f8008-6fb4-5faf-a528-5fd98c80e6c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} - 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160613} {:answer/id #uuid "36cd6545-a02c-55eb-8d8c-b77b5379dd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2} + 2R_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160614} {:answer/id #uuid "