ix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{1}:=4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is an elementary matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc959e6e-5194-5de1-a77f-64a4daedbf96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474750} {:answer/id #uuid "dda0ec43-a72d-5874-9f5d-834317bad33b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474750} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd81130a-839b-50b4-a531-a62146cb8917" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126af85e-564c-5a88-83a5-7aa534682710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474752} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e1d2b-1cc4-5391-9806-84714901dfaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474753} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6983834-6f71-5348-96c0-e1bdfc142faa" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b099eb91-9ca5-5c85-a7d5-72eff2354b80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474754} {:answer/id #uuid "263a88ac-61b5-5e85-ad17-92c76acc9730" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474754} :answer-field/id #uuid "beaa7087-789c-5fc6-91c3-ada531bbfec4" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475303}] :question/id #uuid "73b54284-6d5f-5b76-a388-21fc0778bb8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31889" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $D$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $F$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $E$ is an elementary matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f564662a-a586-5cf0-983d-a463cece18c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474828} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9ec697-d62c-5cd9-a7e3-d0be9a26170b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v